[cot:thought] a sharp 20???22% drop in active correspondents since 2011 and a 10???12% decline in active corridors.
[cot:thought] Latin America saw the steepest fall at 30???34%, followed by small island developing states at roughly 41%. Advanced economies declined by about 23%, while Northern America dropped only 12???13%. The Gini coefficient on active correspondents per corridor sits at 0.75.
[cot:thought] USD relationships fell more sharply than EUR or GBP in 2018. The next step is to review the capture-fisheries theme implementation pattern and build the data module.
[cot:thought] Global corridors fell
[cot:thought] from roughly 10,800 to 9,800. Volume rose while relationships declined, signaling concentration. I will carry forward 2011???2024/2025 trends with caveats.
